A||||8||stsmithgt||I'm having engaging problems with my tranny.||||9||
Z||000000||stsmithgt||12-14-2000||09:01 AM||||It seems to be getting worse.  I've been finding myself sitting at green lights holding up traffic while trying to get my 4 spd. to go into first or even second gear.  This has happened since I had this tranny put in.  I thought I was just not used to the new clutch and replaced tranny, but it's really pissing me off now. Maybe the linkage is out of adjustment.  It also crunches second gear from time to time if I have revved the engine up in first before shifting into second.  I'm not trying to speed shift either.  At first I thought I miss used my clucth, but I'm not sure now.  I was thinking I might be a problem in the clutch, but I didn't want to rule out it may be in the tranny or linkage.  I just had problems getting to work in it this morning.  Something seems to be out of adjustment besides my temper.  I'm afraid I'm going to lose my temper over this ****  and explode this this tranny or snap something trying to get moving from a traffic light.  After all the money I sunk into this area of the car, this is really upsetting me.  This is an 86GT w/4spd.  Well,  I'm done venting for now.  Suggestions?  I think I need to give some folks a call before I loose it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||12-14-2000||06:45 PM||||Sorry to hear of your difficulties.<P>Since it is stubborn about getting into gear while you're stopped, and because it "grinds," I must assume that the clutch is not fully releasing, and the synchro in the trans. are just trying to do their job.<P>My <B>guess</B> is, you should begin by gettin the clutch hydraulics properly bled.  Do a search in the archives, and you'll find plenty of advice on that subject.  Good Luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> - I'll being doing the same thing (for the first time) sometime in the near future. If misery loves company, you'll be in luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000002||Phil||12-14-2000||06:54 PM||||How does it shift with out the engine running? If it shifts through all the gears easily then most likely the trouble is in the hydraulics.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||12-14-2000||06:59 PM||||Could be something as simple a the clutch pedal. <P>My page has several write-ups on clutch problems & cures.  <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/archism.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/archism.htm</A> <P>BTW...One thing for sure, if you don't address the problem right away, it will be a VERY short time before you are replacing the clutch.<P><BR>Archie<P><p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-14-2000||07:12 PM||||Yeah check the peddal but i had the exact same prob. on my 5 speed. When i replace clutch i did not get the linkages right.<BR>would not go into first or third i think.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tom88gt||12-14-2000||07:17 PM||||Check you clutch fluid first.  This is often the cause for many cars.  If full try bleeding the system.||||reg||4
Z||000006||PlasticWrapd||12-14-2000||09:49 PM||||From your description, there can only be three causes:<P>1. The clutch pedal is bent and/or bending. A common problem.  This one is easy.  The clutch pedal should be about one inch <I>higher</I> than the brake pedal when fully released, and there should be <I>no</I> play in the clutch pedal.<P>2. Hydraulic related... The clutch master cylinder and/or slave cylinder needs replacement/rebuild. <P>3.  The clutch pressure plate is separating from the spring diaphragm.  This is a "must replace the clutch" problem.||||reg||1
Z||000007||David Johnson||12-15-2000||08:52 AM||||My  Gt 5 speed is the same way. After I did all the things the other replies are talking about (cluth master cylinder would be the first mechanical thing to check), I found out that it won't synchonize in first.  I keep it in neutral until the light turns yellow then ease it into 2nd so it synchronizes then into first. Don't try to force it.<BR>Good luck<BR>David||||reg||6
Z||000008||stsmithgt||12-15-2000||09:30 AM||||Thanks for all your posts guys.  I don't think it's anything serious.  I'm just trying to find time to work on it.  We've worked about 60 hours this week and I'm a little burnt out.  I'll try and check all that stuff soon as I can.  Thanks again for all your posts.||||reg||7
